IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-child-support-domain`
IMPORT `sg-csp`

§ `The SG Child Support Package, shaped for OpenFisca`

-- WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS.
--
-- sg-csp.l4 is written to be READ AGAINST THE SOURCE: dates are dates, the
-- rule-version axis is explicit, and local bindings name the intermediate
-- quantities a reader needs. That shape is right for review and wrong for
-- `l4 openfisca`, whose v1 lowering supports neither the date builtins
-- (`YMD`, `DATE_YEAR`) nor `WHERE`/`LET` bindings, and which expects the
-- OpenFisca formula shape: an entity and a period in, one number out.
--
-- So this module is a PROJECTION, not a second encoding. It restates the
-- Package's money lines in the subset the exporter accepts, and then
-- ASSERTS ITSELF EQUAL to sg-csp.l4 over a spread of cohorts. If the two
-- ever disagree the assertions fail here, which is the only thing that
-- stops a projection quietly becoming a fork.
--
-- What an agency gets out of it: a runnable OpenFisca module. Agencies that
-- already microsimulate a tax-benefit system in OpenFisca can drop these
-- variables into an existing population model and price the scheme against
-- their own microdata, rather than against the flat per-cohort arithmetic a
-- spreadsheet allows.

§§ `The OpenFisca entity and period`

-- Year-granular ON PURPOSE. Child Credits and the PSEA top-up band on the
-- calendar year the child turns n, so a year is their natural grain. The
-- Baby Gift and the CDA lines band on an exact date, and that is carried by
-- a BOOLEAN the caller sets rather than by a date the exporter cannot read.
DECLARE Person
    HAS `birth year`                            IS A NUMBER
        `born on or after the Package commences` IS A BOOLEAN
        `born on or after the Cash Gift enhancement` IS A BOOLEAN
        `has a Child Development Account`       IS A BOOLEAN
        `birth order`                           IS A NUMBER
        `is a Singapore citizen`                IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Period HAS year IS A NUMBER

@export Total Child Credits a Singapore Citizen child receives under the SG Child Support Package, at $2,000 a year for the years the child turns 1 to 16, counted from 2026 onwards.
GIVEN p      IS A Person @desc The child, with birth year, birth order and citizenship.
      period IS A Period @desc The simulation period.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`child credits` p period MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT p's `is a Singapore citizen` THEN 0
           IF p's `birth year` PLUS 16 LESS THAN 2026 THEN 0
           IF p's `birth year` PLUS 1 AT LEAST 2026 THEN 32000
           OTHERWISE 2000 TIMES (p's `birth year` PLUS 16 MINUS 2025)

@export The $10,000 Post-Secondary Education Account top-up, paid in the year a Singapore Citizen child turns 17, for children turning 17 from 2026 onwards.
GIVEN p      IS A Person @desc The child, with birth year and citizenship.
      period IS A Period @desc The simulation period.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`psea top up` p period MEANS
    IF       p's `is a Singapore citizen`
         AND p's `birth year` PLUS 17 AT LEAST 2026
    THEN 10000
    ELSE 0

@export The Baby Gift line of the SG Child Support Package: $10,000 for a child born on or after 1 April 2027, and for a child still being paid the Baby Bonus Cash Gift on 31 March 2027 the greater of what they have been paid and $10,000. Zero for a cohort the Gift never reaches.
GIVEN p      IS A Person @desc The child. Set the two commencement booleans from the date of birth.
      period IS A Period @desc The simulation period.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`baby gift` p period MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT p's `is a Singapore citizen` THEN 0
           IF p's `born on or after the Package commences` THEN 10000
           IF p's `born on or after the Cash Gift enhancement` THEN 10000
           OTHERWISE 0

@export The Child Development Account First Step Grant under the SG Child Support Package: $5,000 for a Singapore Citizen child born on or after 1 April 2027, and nothing for an existing child, whose grant was paid at birth under whatever scheme then applied.
GIVEN p      IS A Person @desc The child.
      period IS A Period @desc The simulation period.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cda first step grant` p period MEANS
    IF       p's `is a Singapore citizen`
         AND p's `born on or after the Package commences`
    THEN 5000
    ELSE 0

@export The Child Development Account co-matching CAP from 1 October 2027, when every cap becomes $5,000. A cap, not a payment: the Government matches only what the family saves, so an agency pricing this line must apply its own take-up assumption.
GIVEN p      IS A Person @desc The child. `has a Child Development Account` is false for a child born before 1 January 2015, whose account has closed.
      period IS A Period @desc The simulation period.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cda co matching cap` p period MEANS
    IF       p's `is a Singapore citizen`
         AND p's `has a Child Development Account`
    THEN 5000
    ELSE 0

@export default The five lines of the SG Child Support Package added together, for one Singapore Citizen child, birth to 17. The co-matching line is a cap; at full take-up this is the "up to $62,000" of the announcement.
GIVEN p      IS A Person @desc The child.
      period IS A Period @desc The simulation period.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`package total` p period MEANS
         (`baby gift` OF p, period)
    PLUS (`child credits` OF p, period)
    PLUS (`cda first step grant` OF p, period)
    PLUS (`cda co matching cap` OF p, period)
    PLUS (`psea top up` OF p, period)

§§ `The projection asserts itself equal to the encoding it projects`

-- Each pair below is the SAME child, described twice: once as sg-csp.l4's
-- `Child` and once as this module's `Person`. The assertion is that the two
-- descriptions produce the same money. Nothing else keeps a projection
-- honest; a projection that is never compared is a fork nobody declared.

GIVETH A Period
`any year` MEANS Period WITH year IS 2028

GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth order` IS A NUMBER,
      `after commencement` IS A BOOLEAN, `after enhancement` IS A BOOLEAN, `has CDA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Person
`person born` `birth year` `order` `birth order` `flags` `after commencement` `after enhancement` `has CDA` MEANS
    Person WITH
        `birth year` IS `birth year`
        `born on or after the Package commences` IS `after commencement`
        `born on or after the Cash Gift enhancement` IS `after enhancement`
        `has a Child Development Account` IS `has CDA`
        `birth order` IS `birth order`
        `is a Singapore citizen` IS TRUE

GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Child
`child born` `birth year` `order` `birth order` MEANS
    Child WITH
        `name` IS "cross-check"
        `date of birth` IS YMD `birth year` 6 15
        `is a Singapore citizen` IS TRUE
        `birth order` IS `birth order`
        `parents lawfully married` IS TRUE

GIVEN child IS A Child
GIVETH A NUMBER
`encoded lines for` child MEANS
    `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2027 10 1) (`the five Package lines for` child)

-- 2028: a full post-commencement cohort. The headline $62,000.
#ASSERT (`package total` OF (`person born` 2028 `order` 1 `flags` TRUE TRUE TRUE), `any year`) EQUALS 62000
#ASSERT (`package total` OF (`person born` 2028 `order` 1 `flags` TRUE TRUE TRUE), `any year`) EQUALS `encoded lines for` (`child born` 2028 `order` 1)

-- 2026: born before commencement, so no First Step Grant on the Package line.
#ASSERT (`package total` OF (`person born` 2026 `order` 3 `flags` FALSE TRUE TRUE), `any year`) EQUALS `encoded lines for` (`child born` 2026 `order` 3)

-- 2020: before the Cash Gift enhancement, so the Gift line is a dash.
#ASSERT (`package total` OF (`person born` 2020 `order` 1 `flags` FALSE FALSE TRUE), `any year`) EQUALS `encoded lines for` (`child born` 2020 `order` 1)

-- 2012: the account closed at 12, so no co-matching line either.
#ASSERT (`package total` OF (`person born` 2012 `order` 1 `flags` FALSE FALSE FALSE), `any year`) EQUALS `encoded lines for` (`child born` 2012 `order` 1)

-- 2009: the PSEA top-up and nothing else.
#ASSERT (`package total` OF (`person born` 2009 `order` 1 `flags` FALSE FALSE FALSE), `any year`) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT (`package total` OF (`person born` 2009 `order` 1 `flags` FALSE FALSE FALSE), `any year`) EQUALS `encoded lines for` (`child born` 2009 `order` 1)

-- A non-citizen child is outside every line.
`a non-citizen child` MEANS
    Person WITH
        `birth year` IS 2028
        `born on or after the Package commences` IS TRUE
        `born on or after the Cash Gift enhancement` IS TRUE
        `has a Child Development Account` IS TRUE
        `birth order` IS 1
        `is a Singapore citizen` IS FALSE

#ASSERT (`package total` OF `a non-citizen child`, `any year`) EQUALS 0
